# Where the desktop app drops files it could not write straight into the
# repo (it does this whenever the bridge is offline). Copies of real
# source files, at the wrong depth — so tsc tried to compile them and
# reported "Cannot find module '../../lib/supabase'" against a file that
# is not part of the project. Excluded in tsconfig.json too; this keeps
# them out of commits.
Claude outputs/

# FCM / Firebase.
#
# google-services.json is NOT a secret — it ships inside the app and is
# referenced by app.json, so it belongs in the repo. Left tracked
# deliberately; without it, every EAS build fails.
#
# The SERVICE ACCOUNT key is a different thing entirely: it can send a
# push to any user of this project and must never be committed. Upload
# it through `eas credentials` and keep the file out of the repo.
*service-account*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
